    "narrative": "The Ghost Ride the WHIP lineup is anchored today by **Josh Naylor**, whose 77.77 score makes him our premier start. Facing Trey Gibson and his inflated 5.74 xERA, **Josh Naylor** benefits significantly from the combination of a high-ceiling matchup and the favorable hitting environment, further bolstered by a +5% platoon boost. He is joined at the top of the priority list by **Brice Turang** (63.21) and **Cole Young** (60.62). **Cole Young**, in particular, projects as a high-upside play; despite the uncertainty of a pending lineup, his projected lead-off spot against the vulnerable Gibson, combined with a +16% park factor and +19% SP skill advantage, makes him an essential component of our offensive strategy to chase stolen bases and runs.\n\nWe are navigating several risks, most notably the lineup uncertainty for **Travis Bazzana** and **James Wood**, as official orders have yet to be confirmed. **James Wood** faces a challenging assignment against Logan Webb (3.46 xERA), but he remains in the starting slot due to his elite 0.402 xwOBA and a helpful wind-out scenario at the park. Meanwhile, **Jose Caballero** (44.31) and **Tyler Soderstrom** (43.23) occupy our lower-tier start spots; **Jose Caballero** is essentially holding the line against Gavin Williams, though his score was dragged down by an unfavorable platoon and a projected #8 spot in the order. With **Corbin Carroll** off today and both **Mickey Moniak** and **Trevor Story** sidelined on the IL, our depth is being tested, though we are closely monitoring the status of **Austin Riley**, **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Vinnie Pasquantino**, **Max Muncy**, **Gabriel Moreno**, **Carson Williams**, **Zach McKinstry**, **Dalton Rushing**, **Kyle Karros**, **Alex Freeland**, and **Henry Bolte** to ensure we maximize our daily game caps.",
